WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.918 --> 00:00:03.712
If you want to travel. 

00:00:04.087 --> 00:00:06.798
Through indigenous country. 

00:00:08.299 --> 00:00:09.884
Experience the art. 

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:14.723
Whether it's a painting, 

00:00:14.889 --> 00:00:16.349
whether it's a sculpture,

00:00:16.933 --> 00:00:18.560
whether it's a song,

00:00:19.227 --> 00:00:22.397
every piece is the embodiment of a story. 

00:00:23.314 --> 00:00:26.192
The art is the land, 
and the land is the art. 

00:00:26.901 --> 00:00:29.195
This is how we share our stories. 

00:00:31.281 --> 00:00:34.200
I think about my grandfather and father. 

00:00:35.577 --> 00:00:37.996
But everything they had, they had to make. 

00:00:39.831 --> 00:00:42.000
Well, that's who we are, right? 

00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:44.794
We do it every day. 

00:00:46.963 --> 00:00:49.591
We're just connected to the land, 

00:00:49.591 --> 00:00:52.927
because that's how our ancestors were,

00:00:52.927 --> 00:00:54.387
and that's where we came from. 

00:01:00.185 --> 00:01:04.731
It's because we've been making this work for,
you know, thousands of years. 

00:01:05.356 --> 00:01:07.984
You experience our heritage. 

00:01:08.276 --> 00:01:11.613
You experience our culture. 

00:01:11.613 --> 00:01:14.908
You're experiencing how we look at life. 

00:01:16.534 --> 00:01:21.206
In Quebec there's 55 communities, 11 nations. 

00:01:22.874 --> 00:01:25.126
All with distinct practices,

00:01:26.002 --> 00:01:27.170
languages,

00:01:28.046 --> 00:01:30.256
and relationship to the land.

00:01:32.634 --> 00:01:35.011
So to be indigenous is not one thing. 

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:43.353
I just wanted to connect back. 

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:49.901
So I'll beat things that
my grandmother would tell me. 

00:01:50.235 --> 00:01:53.571
I beat a lot of you know,
sacred teachings

00:01:53.571 --> 00:01:56.491
into those sculptures, legends.

00:01:58.326 --> 00:02:01.121
Yeah, there's a lot of stories in there. 

00:02:02.997 --> 00:02:06.292
I think about the younger generation and

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:09.420
we don't want to lose our culture or identity. 

00:02:09.754 --> 00:02:11.297
Stories need to be told,

00:02:11.673 --> 00:02:15.635
and if one can pick it up,
then the culture lives. 

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:18.805
That's traveling. 

00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:22.976
Experiencing the people,
experiencing the stories, 

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:25.937
experiencing the land. 

00:02:26.521 --> 00:02:27.856
Connecting.

